# NOTE (2026-09-18): comment lines in .gitignore MUST start with '#'.
# This file previously used '%' (MATLAB's comment character) for several
# headings -- git does not treat those as comments, it treats them as
# PATTERNS. They matched nothing real so nothing broke, but the file was
# lying about which lines were inert. Fixed throughout.

# --- Regenerable / bulky output folders ---
Figures/
Final Results/
Data/
Legacy/
Pre-rendered Lookup Tables/
Logs/

# --- Machine-local scratch, experiments and superseded code ---
# notes/   : cross-instance investigation write-ups (audits, comparisons).
#            Kept out of the public repo deliberately -- they are working
#            notes between Claude sessions, not documentation for users.
#            README.md stays tracked at the repo root.
# archive/ : superseded or one-off code kept for reference, not for use.
notes/
archive/
configurations.m
*.asv

# --- Local MySQL credentials - never commit, machine-specific ---
mysql_local.json

# --- Regenerable MATLAB derived data ---
# build_ctx.m (DD-RELAX-paper) disk-caches the ambiguity table and atom
# dictionary here, keyed by the grid-affecting config. Each file is tens of
# MB and regenerates automatically in ~65-75s per config. Same reason the
# sibling project's sim/cache is excluded from Syncthing.
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/cache/

# --- Cross-machine batch-collection runners (internal tooling) ---
collectors/

# --- In-development superimposed-pilot DD-RELAX (DD-RELAX-SI) work ---
# Added 2026-10-03 by explicit user instruction: this algorithm family is
# NOT finalized and is NOT to be uploaded to the repo for now.
#
# The flops exemption that used to sit here is LIFTED as of 2026-10-07:
# flops_ddrelaxsi.m and References/DDRelaxSIFlops.lean now exist, so the
# complexity policy is satisfied. The UPLOAD exclusion below still stands
# until the design is final.
#
# Covers the superimposed-pilot variants (SI / SI-DA / SI-GLS / SI-OP),
# the narrow-guard DD-RELAX-L spin-off, and the shared DD-RELAX-paper
# estimator folder they all depend on (dd_relax.m carries the in-progress
# decision-directed full-grid refinement and the fg_trace diagnostic hook;
# the folder also holds the sbl_*.m experiments, likewise unfinished).
# None of these paths was ever tracked, so this is purely preventative.
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/DD-RELAX-paper/
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DDRELAXSI*.m
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DDRELAXL_PTMMSE.m
# Withheld 2026-10-07: this one WAS tracked, but it calls dd_relax,
# build_ctx, oddm_config and build_HDD, which all live in the excluded
# DD-RELAX-paper/ folder above - so the published copy had dangling
# dependencies and could not run from a clean clone. Untracked with
# `git rm --cached`. Publish it together with DD-RELAX-paper/ once the
# design is final.
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DDRELAX_PTMMSE.m

# =====================================================================
# Debug / diagnostic artefacts -- added 2026-10-05 while preparing the
# repo for a public GitHub push. Everything below is either machine-local
# state, run output, or source that explicitly declares itself
# not-for-production. Classified by evidence (file headers and reference
# counts), not by guesswork -- see each note.
# =====================================================================

# --- Editor / assistant session state (machine-local) ---
.claude/

# --- Run logs. `Logs/` is already excluded above; this is the other
#     naming used by the Figure 7 relay collection runs. ---
logs_*/

# --- Sources that declare themselves diagnostic-only in their OWN
#     headers. Both are real, working code that must NOT ship as part of
#     the library, because a user who found them would reasonably assume
#     they were production paths:
#       gen_HDD_direct_slowref.m      "VERIFICATION REFERENCE ONLY ...
#                                      Not for production use."
#       sim_fun_ODDM_OMPPINV_PTMMSE.m "*** DIAGNOSTIC ONLY -- NEVER WIRE
#                                      THIS INTO A PROFILE OR COLLECT
#                                      IT. ***"
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/gen_HDD_direct_slowref.m
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_OMPPINV_PTMMSE.m

# --- Dead DT-MUSIC exploration variants. Each is a suffixed copy of
#     sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSIC_PTMMSE.m from the estimator-tuning work, and
#     NONE is referenced by any profile, by the sim_fun_ODDM_PTMMSE
#     dispatcher, or by any other file (checked: 0 inbound references
#     each). The two LIVE DT-MUSIC files -- sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSIC_PTMMSE.m
#     (2 refs) and sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSICW_PTMMSE.m (5 refs, the
#     "DT-MUSIC-WIN" Figure 7 baseline) -- are deliberately NOT listed
#     here and still ship. Listed individually rather than as a glob so a
#     future real DT-MUSIC variant is not silently hidden.
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSIC2_PTMMSE.m
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSICD_PTMMSE.m
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSICG_PTMMSE.m
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSICGN_PTMMSE.m
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSICO_PTMMSE.m
Comm Functions/ODDM Functions/sim_fun_ODDM_DTMUSICPL_PTMMSE.m

# --- Reference PDFs for the in-development superimposed-pilot work.
#     Excluded for the same reason as its source (see the DD-RELAX-SI
#     block above): that line of work is not being published yet.
#     Reference PDFs in References/ itself are already tracked and keep
#     shipping -- this is only the sub-folder.
References/Superimposed Pilot DD-RELAX/

# --- Generic scratch patterns, so ad-hoc debugging copies never need a
#     new rule here. *.asv is already covered further up. ---
*_backup.m
*_slowref.m
*_prefix.m
scratch/
tmp/

# --- Run artefacts and binary dumps, by file type. Belt and braces: the
#     session scratchpad lives OUTSIDE this tree entirely (under the
#     user's AppData Temp), so it can never be committed from here. These
#     rules only catch an ad-hoc copy made inside the working tree.
*.log
*.mat
*.bak
scratchpad/

# --- Manual audit snapshots (2026-10-12). audits/snapshots/ holds a copy of
#     every file at the moment it passed audit, INCLUDING the unpublished
#     DD-RELAX-SI sources excluded above, so it must never be pushed.
#     audits/AUDIT_LOG.md itself is not ignored. ---
audits/snapshots/

# --- Machine-specific results setup and stores (2026-10-24, public repo prep).
#     A fresh clone has neither file; local_store_setup.m writes both on the
#     first run (a local text store), so they must never be committed. ---
db_sources.json
Results/
mysql_local.json

# --- Unpublished, machine-local profiles (the DD-RELAX family). saved_profiles.m
#     lists them first when the file exists; the public repo ships without it. ---
saved_profiles_local.m

# --- Internal audit records (physics audits of in-development code) ---
audits/

# --- Complexity references and tests whose code lives in the unpublished
#     DD-RELAX-paper/ folder (est_bem, est_nomp, nomp_core, DD-RELAX-SI). ---
References/BEMFlops.lean
References/NOMPFlops.lean
References/DDRelaxSIFlops.lean
tests/validate_nomp_paper.m

